  "requires_revision": true,
  "summary": "The candidate decomposition is largely reasonable and domain-aligned, covering user access, catalog browsing, catalog administration, and media delivery. However, there are two evidence-backed defects: a responsibility overlap between Movie Catalog Service and Catalog Administration Service that fragments what is a single MovieController-backed cohesion, and a likely spurious/unsupported interaction between User Access Service and Media Delivery Service. Neither is fatal, but the overlap and the coupling claims should be reconciled with the evidence before finalizing.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "category": "responsibility_overlap",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Movie Catalog Service and Catalog Administration Service split responsibilities that the static evidence shows are tightly bound. The candidate assigns MovieController to Movie Catalog Service but also claims 'MovieUploadController and admin-only catalog functions' for Catalog Administration. In the code, movie CRUD (register/update/delete, duplicate-title enforcement RF-28/RF-35) is a catalog write concern that shares the same Movie domain/repository consumed by browsing (RF-08..RF-21). The controller package is a single cohesion cluster (5 classes, 25 outgoing edges) and duplicate-title/uniqueness rules straddle both proposed services, creating shared ownership of the Movie entity and its uniqueness invariant.",
      "evidence": [
        "RF-26..RF-33 (catalog administration) plus RF-28/RF-35 uniqueness",
        "static: io.innofang.jokul.controller -> io.innofang.jokul.domain (count=9), controller cluster is single sink",
        "domain business rule: 'Movie title is the unique identifier; duplicate movie titles are prevented'"
      ],
      "recommendation": "Either merge catalog read and write concerns into a single Movie Catalog Service (with admin sub-capability), or clearly designate one owner of the Movie entity and its uniqueness invariant so that title-duplicate enforcement is not split across two services. Justify the split explicitly if administrative write scaling is intended."
    },
    {
      "category": "unsupported_interaction",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "User Access Service is declared to communicate with Media Delivery Service, but there is no evidence in requirements or static dependency edges supporting a direct interaction between authentication/session management and media upload/playback. Playback availability depends on registration and physical file existence (RF-24/25, RNF-62), not on the user service. This appears to be an invented coupling.",
      "evidence": [
        "No requirement links user auth to media delivery",
        "static: no dependency edge from user-related components to utils/properties media handling",
        "RNF-62: playback depends on registration + physical file, not user service"
      ],
      "recommendation": "Remove the User Access Service <-> Media Delivery Service interaction unless an authorization check gates playback/download. If role-based access control gates media, model that as an explicit dependency; otherwise drop it."
    },
    {
      "category": "excessive_coupling",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Media Delivery Service declares communication with all three other services, and Catalog Administration also declares three targets, implying a near-fully-connected mesh. Given the actual coupling in evidence is primarily around movie registration coordinating with file availability (RNF-57 independent-but-related steps), some declared edges (e.g., Media Delivery -> User Access) are not substantiated.",
      "evidence": [
        "candidate: Media Delivery communicates_with all three services",
        "RNF-57: upload and registration are related but independent steps",
        "static edges show controller->utils/properties, not user->media"
      ],
      "recommendation": "Prune interaction lists to those backed by evidence: Media Delivery <-> Catalog Administration (file/registration coordination) and Media Delivery <-> Movie Catalog (playback availability from details). Justify any remaining edges."
    }
  ],
  "preserved_decisions": [
    "Separating User Access Service around UserController and RBAC (RF-01..RF-07, RNF-45..47) is well supported.",
    "Media Delivery Service as a distinct boundary around large MP4 upload, delivery area, and local repository (RNF-48..51, RNF-58/59, RF-22..25) is justified by the utils/properties file-handling cluster and is a coherent domain capability rather than a technical layer."
  ]
}

